Dear Patrik,

I try to answer your questions regarding REddyProc.

> * I can see that the Ustar varies quite a bit between seasons (~0.11 to
> ~0.18) so I'm wondering if there is a way of using the seasonal values
> in the gapfilling instead of the annually aggregated ones? Without
> splitting up the data sets and do multiple runs that is.
That is straightforward.
see function usGetSeasonalSeasonUStarMappingFromDistributionResult
to be provided to sMDSGapFillAfterUstar with argument UstarThres.df

Explained also with the vignette using data from an agricultural site:
vignette("DEGebExample")

> * How do I do the bootstrapping if I run this example code manually?
> Maybe it's already performed but I don't see it in the output files?
It is hard to give general advice for manual bootstrapping. For
REddyProc, good starting point is to look at the implementation of
sEstUstarThresholdDistribution
at r-forge
https://r-forge.r-project.org/scm/viewvc.php/pkg/REddyProc/R/EddyUStarFilterDP.R?root=reddyproc&view=log

> * In the version 1 above, I'm trying to "plot saturation of NEE with
